WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.204 --> 00:00:18.005
Marilla had decided to keep Anne, but she didn't want to tell Anne until the next day.

2
00:00:18.645 --> 00:00:25.047
She took Anne upstairs and said, "Now, Anne, I noticed you threw all your clothes on the floor.

3
00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.208
That's a bad habit.

4
00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:30.290
Please fold your clothes and put them on the chair."

5
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:34.352
"I was so upset last night I forgot," said Anne.

6
00:00:34.372 --> 00:00:36.774
"I'll fold them nicely tonight."

7
00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:39.436
"Say your prayers and get into bed."

8
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:43.478
"I never say any prayers," announced Anne.

9
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:45.540
Marilla was horrified.

10
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.021
"What do you mean?

11
00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.183
Were you never taught to say prayers?"

12
00:00:50.203 --> 00:00:51.984
"Well, Mrs.

13
00:00:52.044 --> 00:00:55.426
Thomas told me that God made my hair red on purpose.

14
00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.628
So I don't really care for God.

15
00:00:58.268 --> 00:01:01.069
Anyway, I'm always too tired to say prayers."

16
00:01:01.089 --> 00:01:05.491
"Well, you must say your prayers here," Marilla insisted.

17
00:01:05.511 --> 00:01:08.972
"Of course I will," said Anne cheerfully.

18
00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:10.013
"I'm ready.

19
00:01:10.573 --> 00:01:11.313
What do I say?"

20
00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:16.556
"Just thank God and ask for some things you want," Marilla told Anne.

21
00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.617
"I'll do my best," promised Anne.

22
00:01:19.637 --> 00:01:25.759
"Dear God, thank you for the wild cherry tree and the lake, which I call 'the Lake of

23
00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:26.980
Shining Waters.'

24
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.202
I want so many things that it'll take a long time to say everything.

25
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:37.767
So the most important things are these: please let me stay at Green Gables and please make me

26
00:01:37.867 --> 00:01:39.128
pretty when I grow up."

27
00:01:40.589 --> 00:01:44.732
Marilla waited until the next afternoon to tell Anne she could stay.

28
00:01:45.512 --> 00:01:51.076
During the morning Marilla asked Anne to do various tasks, and she watched Anne with a keen eye.

29
00:01:51.716 --> 00:01:58.073
By noon Marilla saw that Anne was a hard worker, quick to learn, clever, and obedient.

30
00:01:58.853 --> 00:02:04.517
Her most serious shortcoming was a tendency to start daydreaming in the middle of a task and forget

31
00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.619
everything until Marilla reprimanded her.

32
00:02:07.519 --> 00:02:10.961
When Anne finished washing dishes, she suddenly grabbed Marilla.

33
00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:15.605
"Oh please, Miss Cuthbert, can you tell me if I can stay or not?

34
00:02:16.325 --> 00:02:18.347
I've tried to be patient all morning.

35
00:02:18.987 --> 00:02:19.908
Please tell me."

36
00:02:19.928 --> 00:02:24.651
"You haven't rinsed the dishcloth in boiling water, Anne," said Marilla.

37
00:02:24.671 --> 00:02:26.092
"Do that first."

38
00:02:26.808 --> 00:02:30.030
Anne attended to the dishcloth and then looked at Marilla again.

39
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:37.215
"Well," said Marilla, "Matthew and I decided to keep you— if you are a good girl.

40
00:02:38.036 --> 00:02:39.617
Anne, what's the matter?"

41
00:02:39.637 --> 00:02:44.160
"I'm crying," said Anne, "but I don't know why.

42
00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.101
I'm so happy.

43
00:02:46.121 --> 00:02:48.863
Oh, happy isn't the right word.

44
00:02:49.504 --> 00:02:52.926
I was happy to see the trees and flowers—but this!

45
00:02:53.587 --> 00:02:55.288
I'll try to be so good.

46
00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.163
Mrs. Thomas said I am wicked, so it will be difficult, but I'll try.

47
00:03:00.183 --> 00:03:02.725
But why am I crying, Marilla?"

48
00:03:02.745 --> 00:03:08.368
"I suppose because you're excited and worked up," said Marilla disapprovingly.

49
00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.470
"Sit down on that chair.

50
00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.091
Try to calm down.

51
00:03:12.671 --> 00:03:14.613
You laugh and cry far too easily.

52
00:03:15.313 --> 00:03:18.535
Now, you must go to school when it starts in September.

53
00:03:19.196 --> 00:03:21.197
Until then you can help me here."

54
00:03:21.217 --> 00:03:22.938
"What will I call you?

55
00:03:23.538 --> 00:03:24.299
Miss Cuthbert?

56
00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:25.600
Aunt Marilla?"

57
00:03:26.224 --> 00:03:27.645
"No, just Marilla.

58
00:03:28.185 --> 00:03:29.826
I'm not used to Miss Cuthbert.

59
00:03:30.406 --> 00:03:32.187
Just plain Marilla is fine."

60
00:03:32.207 --> 00:03:37.949
"It sounds awfully disrespectful to say just Marilla," protested Anne.

61
00:03:37.969 --> 00:03:39.569
"Everybody else does.

62
00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.331
Make sure you speak politely, and it will be fine," Marilla replied.

63
00:03:44.351 --> 00:03:48.773
"I'd love to call you Aunt Marilla," said Anne.

64
00:03:48.793 --> 00:03:54.095
"I've never had an aunt or any relation at all, not even a grandmother.

65
00:03:54.115 --> 00:03:57.365
Please?" "No, you can't.

66
00:03:57.985 --> 00:04:01.007
I don't believe in calling people names that don't belong to them."

67
00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.708
"But we could imagine you're my aunt."

68
00:04:03.728 --> 00:04:06.850
"I couldn't," said Marilla grimly.

69
00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:11.293
"Do you ever imagine things different from what they really are, Marilla?"

70
00:04:11.693 --> 00:04:13.014
asked Anne, wide-eyed.

71
00:04:13.034 --> 00:04:15.595
"No," said Marilla.

72
00:04:15.615 --> 00:04:18.837
"Oh!" Anne drew a long breath.

73
00:04:19.537 --> 00:04:20.338
Then she spoke.

74
00:04:20.358 --> 00:04:23.540
"Oh, Marilla, how much you miss!"

75
00:04:25.252 --> 00:04:31.335
Later Anne asked, "Marilla, do you think I will ever have a kindred spirit in Avonlea?"

76
00:04:31.355 --> 00:04:33.417
"A a what?"

77
00:04:33.937 --> 00:04:34.597
asked Marilla.

78
00:04:34.617 --> 00:04:41.241
"A kindred spirit, a best friend in whom I can confide my innermost soul.

79
00:04:41.861 --> 00:04:44.062
I've dreamed of meeting her all my life.

80
00:04:44.703 --> 00:04:49.846
I never really supposed I would, but so many of my dreams have come true all at once

81
00:04:49.926 --> 00:04:51.987
that perhaps this one will too.

82
00:04:52.547 --> 00:04:53.888
Do you think it's possible?"

83
00:04:54.848 --> 00:04:59.409
"Diana Barry lives nearby, and she's about your age," Marilla replied.

84
00:04:59.429 --> 00:05:05.571
"She's a very nice girl, and perhaps she can be your playmate when she comes home.

85
00:05:06.351 --> 00:05:07.691
She's visiting her aunt now.

86
00:05:08.292 --> 00:05:10.732
You'll have to be careful how you behave though.

87
00:05:11.312 --> 00:05:13.553
Mrs. Barry is very particular.

88
00:05:14.293 --> 00:05:18.254
She won't let Diana play with any girl who isn't nice and good."

89
00:05:18.274 --> 00:05:20.755
"What is Diana like?"

90
00:05:21.315 --> 00:05:21.915
Anne asked.

91
00:05:22.575 --> 00:05:24.216
"Her hair isn't red, is it?

92
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.221
Oh, I hope not.

93
00:05:26.821 --> 00:05:32.965
It's bad enough to have red hair myself, but I positively couldn't endure it in a best friend

94
00:05:33.086 --> 00:05:37.308
too." "Diana is a very pretty girl," said Marilla.

95
00:05:37.328 --> 00:05:40.811
"She has black eyes and hair and rosy cheeks.

96
00:05:41.651 --> 00:05:45.854
And she is good and smart, which is better than being pretty."

97
00:05:45.874 --> 00:05:49.717
"I'm so glad she's pretty," Anne said.

98
00:05:49.737 --> 00:05:54.360
"I'm not beautiful, so having a beautiful friend would be wonderful.

99
00:05:55.028 --> 00:05:56.089
When I lived with Mrs.

100
00:05:56.149 --> 00:05:59.051
Thomas, there was a bookcase with glass doors.

101
00:05:59.832 --> 00:06:01.713
One of the doors was broken because Mr.

102
00:06:01.733 --> 00:06:03.694
Thomas smashed it when he was drunk.

103
00:06:04.335 --> 00:06:06.196
The other glass door was whole.

104
00:06:06.877 --> 00:06:10.980
I used to pretend that my reflection was another little girl who lived in the glass.

105
00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:15.002
"Her name was Katie, and we were very close.

106
00:06:15.663 --> 00:06:17.084
I told her everything.

107
00:06:17.604 --> 00:06:19.406
Katie was my only friend.

108
00:06:20.026 --> 00:06:22.548
We pretended that the bookcase was enchanted.

109
00:06:23.132 --> 00:06:25.634
I knew the spell that took me to Katie's world.

110
00:06:26.194 --> 00:06:32.819
In Katie's world there were flowers and fairies and sunshine, and we would live there happily ever after.

111
00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.661
When I went to live with Mrs.

112
00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:37.643
Hammond, I was so upset to leave Katie.

113
00:06:38.363 --> 00:06:39.644
She was sad too."

114
00:06:40.805 --> 00:06:44.148
Marilla listened and then gave Anne a strange look.

115
00:06:44.168 --> 00:06:46.590
"I don't approve of such things, Anne.

116
00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.652
You seem to half-believe your own imagination.

117
00:06:50.284 --> 00:06:50.964
Don't let Mrs.

118
00:06:51.024 --> 00:06:53.265
Barry hear you talking about your friend Katie.

119
00:06:53.865 --> 00:06:55.265
She'll think you're strange."

120
00:06:55.285 --> 00:06:57.666
"Oh, I won't," said Anne.

121
00:06:57.686 --> 00:06:59.447
"I won't tell anybody.

122
00:07:00.007 --> 00:07:01.587
But I thought you'd like to know."

123
00:07:01.607 --> 00:07:04.788
"Well," Marilla said, smiling.

124
00:07:04.808 --> 00:07:07.629
"You'll have a real friend soon, Anne."

125
00:07:07.649 --> 00:07:11.230
"Look, there's a big bee in that apple blossom!"

126
00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.230
said Anne.

127
00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:17.472
"If I wasn't human, I think I'd like to be a bee and live in the flowers!"

128
00:07:18.312 --> 00:07:21.535
"Yesterday you wanted to be a bird," said Marilla.

129
00:07:21.555 --> 00:07:23.877
"You are very fickle.

130
00:07:24.457 --> 00:07:26.539
Now just be quiet for a minute!

131
00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:31.704
It seems impossible for you to stop talking if you've got anybody who will listen to you!"
